            "review_text": "jillianferguson315\nKuala Lumpur, Malaysia11 contributions\n1\nA great surprise!\nJun 2018 • Couples\nWe searched bars with live music and found that this place was suggested. When we turned up on the street, we couldn’t hear much and were suspicious, however as soon as we entered we were met by a crowd of people having the time of their lives!\n\nWe stayed to see two bands. The first were great and everyone was singing along. The second were fantastic too, and performed current English songs and Vietnamese songs (which were catchy despite us not knowing what was going on!). The second band had a beat boxer who was incredible!\n \nYou get your drinks at the bar, and then stand and join in the fun - either dance your socks off or stand with your drink and giving it laldi with a head nod or two.\n\nOne thing that really struck me was the crowd. People were obviously drinking lots and letting loose, but they were so friendly. Whenever anyone bumped into us by mistake, they were so quick to apologise! This is surprising as most of the time drunk people don’t realise! We were also greeted warmly by strangers and welcomed to the place.\n\nThis is a great place, and hidden gem for the locals. We were delighted to stumble across it and had such a good Saturday night! If you want to find somewhere with live music then go for it. Lots of stuff to sing along too, and they mash up songs as well.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten June 2, 2018",
