            "review_text": "Kevyn S\n51 contributions\n0\nFinally, voices that rock !\nJun 2015 • Friends\nSo, I have been to several live music venues here in HCMC over the last 3 years and a majority of them seem to consist of your run-of-the-mill C-list Karaoke Bar singers on steroids. Thankfully Fang came into my life.\n\nThe crowd is a little younger (college-aged to mid-20's) and the drinks are a little pricey - I'm sure that I get the foreigner price for my Jameson - for the type of selection, but some times higher prices is the number deterent for the hammerheads expecting $10,000 VND beers like they get down on Hammerhead Row Bui Vien \n\nThe music and tight confines really make this place a good night. I have visited a handful of times this summer and each time the women vocalists really rock it. There is one heavy-set male vocalist with long hair that is off the charts tight. A few times when I have gone on the weekday the singers tend to let their buddies join them for a few songs and it turns into a bad buddy party. As long as the there's a crowd the singers will jam. They really seem to be trained pros tapped into their voices from their hearts and stomachs. You know, too ofthen in this town you hear that mono-toned high pitch voice that never leaves the forehead. Not that i can sing....\n\nk-\nRead more\nValue\nService\nWritten July 2, 2015",
